sweet ufs: cache partition lookups, report where a lookup blocks

The modem asks sweet_ufs_part() for "misc"/"efs"/"modem" again on every
rmtfs request, and each call probed up to eight LUNs while holding
sweet_ufs_lock; a LUN with no device costs a SCSI timeout, and the whole
system (HFS, the log flusher, the console queue behind them) waits for the
lock. On bp13 a run that had flushed four times then sat at "lk 1/1 st 1"
for a minute with no command outstanding, i.e. inside such a lookup.

Cache every answer (misses too), answer the root partition from the state
sweet_ufs_init already has, probe the LUN that answered last time first,
and keep part_lun/part_step in the heartbeat (pp <lun>/<step>) so a lookup
that never returns names its own LUN and stage. Probes are logged after the
lock is dropped.

